## 1. Frontend: Rendering Efficiency & State Management

### A. Keystroke Render Storms in Input Forms
In multiple user-facing forms, text input updates trigger a complete component-wide re-render on every keystroke. Because these components render heavy children (such as complex Markdown elements via `ReactMarkdown`, YouTube search result guides, and detailed checklists), typing experiences are sluggish.

*   **File References:**
    *   [Troubleshoot.tsx:L219-L225](file:///C:/dev/vibe-mechanic/src/components/Troubleshoot.tsx#L219-L225) (binding of the `symptoms` textarea)
    *   [Obd2Lookup.tsx:L299-L302](file:///C:/dev/vibe-mechanic/src/components/Obd2Lookup.tsx#L299-L302) (binding of the `codeQuery` input)
    *   [PartScanner.tsx:L377-L379](file:///C:/dev/vibe-mechanic/src/components/PartScanner.tsx#L377-L379) (binding of the `userContext` textarea)
*   **Issues:**
    *   `ReactMarkdown` is computationally expensive to parse and re-render. On every single keypress of the `symptoms` input, the entire existing diagnostic report (if displayed) is parsed and rendered from scratch.
    *   In [Obd2Lookup.tsx](file:///C:/dev/vibe-mechanic/src/components/Obd2Lookup.tsx), the inline SVG drawing for the 16-pin connector layout is re-evaluated on every keystroke.
*   **Recommended Fix:**
    *   Isolate form inputs into their own small components, use uncontrolled inputs with `useRef` for submission, or wrap heavy display sections (like Markdown renderers or SVG diagrams) in `React.memo` or `useMemo`.
    ```tsx
    // Memoize the markdown result to prevent re-renders when typing follow-ups
    const MemoizedMarkdown = React.memo(({ content }: { content: string }) => (
      <ReactMarkdown>{content}</ReactMarkdown>
    ));
    ```

### B. Redundant Network Fetches on Tab Navigation
The main layout utilizes conditional tab switching, which fully unmounts and remounts components when switching views.
*   **File References:**
    *   [App.tsx:L94-L99](file:///C:/dev/vibe-mechanic/src/App.tsx#L94-L99) (conditional rendering of tabs)
    *   [SpecsAndService.tsx:L225-L228](file:///C:/dev/vibe-mechanic/src/components/SpecsAndService.tsx#L225-L228) (`useEffect` hook auto-fetching specs and maintenance data)
*   **Issues:**
    *   When a user selects the "Specs & Guides" tab, it fetches vehicle specifications and maintenance logs. If the user navigates away (e.g., to "Diagnose") and returns to "Specs & Guides", the component remounts, triggering redundant network fetches to the Gemini API.
    *   This consumes unnecessary Gemini API tokens, triggers backend rate limits, and frustrates the user with repeating loading spinners.
*   **Recommended Fix:**
    *   Lift the data state up to `App.tsx` or wrap the app in a cache context. Alternatively, hide the tabs using CSS visibility toggles (`hidden` class) instead of unmounting them, or employ a library like TanStack Query with a configured cache time (`staleTime`).

