## 3. Frontend & Backend: Payload Sizing

### A. Uncompressed High-Res Vision Uploads
When users capture or upload vehicle part photos for vision analysis, the raw image is read and transmitted as a massive base64 string.
*   **File References:**
    *   [PartScanner.tsx:L137-L149](file:///C:/dev/vibe-mechanic/src/components/PartScanner.tsx#L137-L149) (image file upload handler)
    *   [PartScanner.tsx:L160-L172](file:///C:/dev/vibe-mechanic/src/components/PartScanner.tsx#L160-L172) (vision endpoint submit)
*   **Issues:**
    *   Modern smartphones capture photos ranging from 5MB to 15MB. Transmitting a raw 12MP base64 string over a cellular connection (common for roadside troubleshooting) results in high network latency, failed uploads, and excessive memory utilization on the client.
    *   Gemini Vision does not require high-resolution inputs to perform parts classification; images resized to 1024x1024 px yield identical diagnostic accuracy.
*   **Recommended Fix:**
    *   Perform client-side image compression and resizing using an offscreen canvas element before converting it to base64. Limit dimensions to a maximum of 1024px and compress to a JPEG with 0.8 quality. This reduces payload sizes by **~98%** (down to ~150-200KB).
    ```typescript
    // Helper to resize base64 images
    function resizeImage(base64Str: string, maxDim = 1024): Promise<string> {
      return new Promise((resolve) => {
        const img = new Image();
        img.src = base64Str;
        img.onload = () => {
          const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
          let width = img.width;
          let height = img.height;
          if (width > height) {
            if (width > maxDim) {
              height *= maxDim / width;
              width = maxDim;
            }
          } else {
            if (height > maxDim) {
              width *= maxDim / height;
              height = maxDim;
            }
          }
          canvas.width = width;
          canvas.height = height;
          const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
          ctx?.drawImage(img, 0, 0, width, height);
          resolve(canvas.toDataURL('image/jpeg', 0.8));
        };
      });
    }
    ```

